    <DataNode elementId="AT2G47180-MONOMER" textLabel="AT2G47180-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT2G47180-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="555" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">GolS1 is a galactinol synthase. When, the GolS1 gene was heterologously expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; as a GST-fusion protein, the purified GST-fusion protein was shown to catalyze the synthesis of galactinol from &lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol and UDP-galactose |CITS:[11846875]|. The same activity was observed when GolS1 was overexpressed in Arabidopsis plants |CITS: [18502973]|. GolS1 transcript levels rise in response to methyl viologen, an oxidative damage-inducing agent. Plants over-expressing GolS1 have increased tolerance to salt, chilling, and high-light stress |CITS: [18502973]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G47180-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-27" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT2G47180.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
